{
  "statement": "The nightly pass labels each dated thing of its member's with what kind of date it is and how much it needs beforehand, and the memory pass dates a birthday or an anniversary they keep, so offload can remind them at the right moments. Things kept for keeping, routines, facts with a date and their own birthday get nothing. A note's name is copied from its own words.",
  "why": "A table turns the two labels into reminder times, so a wrong label is a reminder at the wrong moment or one that never comes. The owner's examples are the bar: a wife's birthday a month and five days out, a meeting just before, a visa before a trip a month away.",
  "sources": [
    "042 AC-1 to AC-5, AC-24",
    "nightly.md: Reminders",
    "memory.md: Dates that come round every year",
    "nightly.py: listing, labels_wire",
    "memories.py: dates_wire"
  ],
  "cases": [
